f Antonio Almeida, Past EHA President\\nHospital da Luz, Lisbon\\n“Borderless Hematology is about giving the best quality of care to all hematology patients.”\\nProf Antonio Almeida, Past EHA President\\nHospital da Luz, Lisbon\\nBecome an EHA Mentor\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"web-83e60321c54d77fceac7525a\", \"title\": \"Work at EHA - The European Hematology Association (EHA)Work at EHA - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 4021, \"end\": 5621, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 1600}], \"navigation_excerpt\": true, \"text\": \"Jobs that match your ambition\\nEHA is a not-for-profit organization that’s on a mission to transform hematology by mobilizing the community, sharing knowledge, and connecting interests. We advocate for hematology in Europe—and beyond. We seek team members, based in the Netherlands, who are creative, driven to achieve excellence, and inspired by our vision of achieving Borderless Hematology.\\nHead of Education\\nOctober 30, 2026\\nHybrid\\nAre you experienced in CME development and up-to-date with educational programs, and ready to join a vibrant association serving 12.000 members? Join EHA as Head of Education.\\nSee vacancy\\nTemp. Membership Engagement Manager\\nOctober 23, 2026\\nHybrid\\nWorking at the heart of membership engagement? Apply and join EHA as Membership Engagement Manager.\\nSee vacancy\\nEHA Intern – Program Management\\nOctober 21, 2026\\nHybrid\\nAn international internship opportunity where you will support the Senior Program Manager in charge of Congress and Scientific Meetings.\\nSee vacancy\\nEHA Internship – Open Application\\nJuly 12, 2026\\nHybrid\\nAre you looking for an internship opportunity where you make a positive impact to the international Hematology landscape?\\nSee vacancy\\n“At EHA, each voice matters, each idea is valued, and together we strive to transform the landscape of hematology—empowering progress, advancing discovery, and building a future where care knows no borders.”\\nRob\\nHead of Operations\\n“After losing my dad to leukemia in 2024, I felt eager to use my skills and experience to make a meaningful impact for patients, caregivers, and doctors in the field of hematology.\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"web-307533c1a4508473094316ab\", \"title\": \"Empowering progress, knowledge, and partnership. - The European Hematology Association (EHA)Empowering progress, knowledge, and partnership. - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 4142, \"end\": 5742, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 1600}], \"navigation_excerpt\": true, \"text\": \"Empowering progress, knowledge, and partnership.\\nWelcome to Borderless Hematology.\\nEHA is the leading force in hematology, bringing the community together to share knowledge, collaborate, connect, and grow.\\nTogether we accelerate progress through education, science, and innovation. Together we improve patient outcomes and progress towards cures—across Europe and beyond.\\nTogether, the future of hematology is within our reach.\\nJoin us with membership that works for you or learn more about our story.\\nEHA2027 Congress\\nEuropean affairs\\nEHA Campus\\nGrants\\nSpecialized Working Groups\\nWhat’s new?\\nGo to overview\\nTuesday, September 29, 2026\\nEHA's Long-Term Advocacy for Hematology Achieves a Major Milestone\\nTuesday, September 22, 2026\\nInterview with EHA’s European Affairs Committee Member, Ariane Weinman\\nThursday, July 23, 2026\\nASCERTAIN project for better pricing and reimbursement models enters final phase\\nWednesday, July 22, 2026\\nInterview with EHA’s European Affairs Committee Member, Kate Morgan\\nMonday, July 6, 2026\\nPublication of EHA Annual General Meeting 2026 minutes\\nReady to join our community?\\nOur network is not just a professional association; it’s a community that nurtures growth, membership, and innovation in a manner that transcends geographical and intellectual borders. To us, this is Borderless Hematology.\\nJoin EHA today\\nEHA Mentorship Program\\nBecome a mentor today\\nMentoring is about more than sharing knowledge. It’s about building connections, gaining fresh perspectives, and helping shape the future of hematology.\\nIf you believe in the power of community and want to suppo\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"web-f3aba4b966c28f155f997043\", \"title\": \"Grants - The European Hematology Association (EHA)Grants - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 3974, \"end\": 5007, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 1033}, {\"start\": 5248, \"end\": 5268, \"excerpt_start\": 1034, \"excerpt_end\": 1054}], \"navigation_excerpt\": true, \"text\": \"Grants\\nEHA’s foundations are built upon our belief that it’s the collective endeavors of our community—in research and clinical practice—that lead to exponential advancements.\\nWe’re committed to accelerating progress in hematology by promoting collaboration, education, and research across all levels.\\nAn important way of achieving this is through the careful and selective allocation of grants and funding to aspiring scientists and researchers.\\nTo check which of our grants you can apply for, use the filters below. Alternatively, you can read about our different grant categories:\\nEHA Research Grants\\nEHA Bilateral Collaborative Grant\\nEHA Innovation Grant\\nEHA Kick-off Grant\\nEHA Research Mobility Grant\\nIn this section, you can also learn about EHA Travel Grants, funding from non-EHA sources and browse our grant-winners hall of fame.\\nEHA Advanced Research Grant\\nEHA Bilateral Collaborative Grant\\nEHA Innovation Grant\\nEHA Junior Research Grant\\nEHA Kick-off Grant\\nEHA Physician Scientist Research Grant\\nEHA Research Mobility Grant\\nBecome an EHA Mentor\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"web-81c57feef95692fb83b63747\", \"title\": \"EHA Bilateral Collaborative Grant - The European Hematology Association (EHA)EHA Bilateral Collaborative Grant - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 4082, \"end\": 4115, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 33}, {\"start\": 4184, \"end\": 4239, \"excerpt_start\": 34, \"excerpt_end\": 89}, {\"start\": 4578, \"end\": 6090, \"excerpt_start\": 90, \"excerpt_end\": 1602}], \"navigation_excerpt\": true, \"text\": \"EHA Bilateral Collaborative Grant\\nLeft Sidebar\\n3 min read · May 6, 2025\\nMay 6, 2025\\nShare\\nThe call has closed. Winners will be announced by mid-April 2027.\\nEHA Bilateral Collaborative Grants support collaboration between two independent research groups with complementarity of expertise and showing a mutual need to answer a specific research question.\\nSuccessful applicants can receive up to €320,000 for two years to be divided equally between the two research groups .\\nEligibility\\nYou’re eligible if:\\nBoth principal investigators (PIs) are EHA members\\nBoth PIs are basic and/or translational researchers\\nBoth PIs are independent researchers or group leaders and have full appointments at academic institutes or proven equivalents\\nThe PIs conduct their research in two different countries in Europe\\nAt least one of the PIs is a junior independent group leader, within five years of conducting independent research\\nNote: If an applicant is a physician scientist, at least 50% of their time should be dedicated to lab research\\nUnfortunately, you are not eligible if your proposal relates to:\\nPurely clinical research projects\\nProjects in health economics\\nOther non-lab-based research\\nTopics-in-Focus Bilateral Collaborative Grants: If your research focuses on hemoglobinopathies, you will have a competitive advantage in the selection process. Please select the ‘Topics-in-Focus Bilateral Collaborative Grant’ on your application form.\\nExtending the reach of our grants: If you are operating in a country less-represented among EHA grantees, you will have a competitive advantage in the selection proce\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"web-9bdd70664e43e95f6f2247c0\", \"title\": \"Topics-in-Focus program - The European Hematology Association (EHA)Topics-in-Focus program - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 4042, \"end\": 4964, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 922}, {\"start\": 5205, \"end\": 5225, \"excerpt_start\": 923, \"excerpt_end\": 943}], \"navigation_excerpt\": true, \"text\": \"Topics-in-Focus program\\nSupport for a changing world.\\nWith advancements in medical technology and research, there’s never been a more exciting time to be involved in hematology.\\nAs pioneers in our field, our role is to lead the change and find novel ways to incorporate new techniques and therapies into daily practice. We need to rapidly deploy these innovations to fuel our advance towards prevention, a cure, and improved quality of life.\\nOverview\\nEHA launched the Topics-in-Focus program to provide support and guidance to hematologists and amplify efforts by focusing on a specific disease related or area related topics to provide better access to innovation.\\nThe program is designed to:\\nRaise awareness\\nProvide education\\nDevelop further research frameworks and access\\nBuild a network of experts in specific focus areas\\nThe program has two strands, each with a specific theme:\\nPrecision hematology\\nHemoglobinopathies\\nBecome an EHA Mentor\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"web-88851fc8d85e155717517ebd\", \"title\": \"HemaSphere - The European Hematology Association (EHA)HemaSphere - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 3990, \"end\": 4000, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 10}, {\"start\": 4039, \"end\": 4100, \"excerpt_start\": 11, \"excerpt_end\": 72}, {\"start\": 4192, \"end\": 5721, \"excerpt_start\": 73, \"excerpt_end\": 1602}], \"navigation_excerpt\": true, \"text\": \"HemaSphere\\nLeft Sidebar\\n3 min read · April 30, 2025\\nApril 30, 2025\\nShare\\nStay at the forefront of cutting-edge research with EHA’s open access, peer-reviewed journal.\\nWith a preliminary 2025 Impact Factor of 11.3, placing it #8 in indexed hematology journals worldwide, HemaSphere is an invaluable resource for hematologists at every career stage.\\nOur continuous online publications support the global hematology community by sharing:\\nResults of high-impact basic, translational, and clinical hematology research\\nInsightful review articles\\nClinical practice guidelines\\nReports of new therapies\\nRecommendations for future research and clinical applications\\nDiscussions on European policy\\nAnd more\\nWe also provide the hematology community with a friction-free route to publishing and publication access through our:\\nFast and constructive review process\\n100% open access content\\nLow publication fees\\nLatest issue\\nExplore this month’s HemaSphere issue, featuring a broad range of hematology papers and insightful discussions on trending topics.\\nHemaSphere podcast\\nListen to the latest HemaSphere podcast and enjoy lighthearted conversations about the research stories behind the publications.\\nThis audio companion to our official journal is available on a range of podcast platforms, and we launch new episodes regularly.\\nCall for novel findings\\nHemaSphere is interested in high-impact studies that share novel findings.\\nIf your study fits this description, please feel free to submit it online for our consideration. HemaSphere does not charge any submission fees.\\nDiscounted publishing fees for EHA membe\"}], \"local_exploration\": {\"visited_doc_ids\": [\"web-307533c1a4508473094316ab\", \"web-f3aba4b966c28f155f997043\", \"web-e00b0a496819dad9ea1b68ec\", \"web-81c57feef95692fb83b63747\", \"web-fa499d75bb6176a42b1557b3\", \"web-9bdd70664e43e95f6f2247c0\", \"web-9e620f66ae71fe39b118f492\", \"web-88851fc8d85e155717517ebd\", \"web-83e60321c54d77fceac7525a\", \"web-cbefd1c2c3a09225cc1843c0\", \"web-ece509e1ea7055ce41222f0b\"], \"visited_pages\": [{\"doc_id\": \"web-307533c1a4508473094316ab\", \"url\": \"https://ehaweb.org/\", \"title\": \"Empowering 